# Vector basemap style URLs (MapLibre style JSON) from the self-hosted tile server (ops/deploy/linux/maps:
# Martin + Caddy under /tiles). Leave them unset: the app then loads the same files from its own origin
# (/tiles/styles/{liberty,positron,dark}.json), which is right for production, the test instance and any copy of
# this file. There is no outside default (G8). Do not point a dev or test copy at the production site: /tiles sends
# no CORS headers, so maps fail, and it sends test traffic to production.
# Local development without Martin shows blank maps. A developer may opt in to a public style host (e.g. OpenFreeMap)
# explicitly in .env.local, never in .env; `npm run build` fails if an outside map host ends up in the bundle.
# Example, a local tile server (absolute URLs only when the tiles are on another origin):
# VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=http://localhost:8099/tiles/styles/liberty.json
# VITE_MAP_STYLE_LIGHT=http://localhost:8099/tiles/styles/positron.json
# VITE_MAP_STYLE_DARK=http://localhost:8099/tiles/styles/dark.json
# Font for marker labels and cluster counts; must exist on the style's glyph server.
VITE_MAP_FONT=Noto Sans Bold
